<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8"/>
		<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" type="image/png"/>
		<title>FAQ - Wrapper: Offline</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Frequently asked questions about Wrapper: Offline"/>
		<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/pages/css/global.css">
		<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/pages/css/faq.css">
		<script src="/pages/js/jquery.js"></script>
		<script src="/pages/js/global.js"></script>
	</head>

	<body>
		<%~ includeFile("./includes/header", { env: it.env }) %>

		<main class="faq-page">
			<div class="faq-intro">
				<h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
				<p>Quick answers about creating videos, managing your projects, and using Wrapper: Offline.</p>
			</div>

			<section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-projects">
				<h2 id="faq-projects">Videos and projects</h2>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I create a video?</summary>
					<p>Select <strong>Make a Video</strong> in the header, choose a theme, and create your project in the video maker. Your saved videos appear in <strong>My Videos</strong>.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I upload an existing movie?</summary>
					<p>Choose <strong>Upload a Movie</strong> in the header and select a Wrapper movie ZIP containing <code>movie.xml</code>. The imported project is added to My Videos.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>What is the Archive?</summary>
					<p>The Archive keeps videos separate from My Videos without deleting them. Use the archive/restore action on a video to move it between the two views.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I find one of my videos?</summary>
					<p>Use the search box on the video list to search by part or all of a video's name or ID. Search applies to the selected view: My Videos or Archive.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I continue editing a saved video?</summary>
					<p>Open <strong>My Videos</strong> and select the edit action on the video you want to continue. You can also search by its title or ID first.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How can I preview or download a video project?</summary>
					<p>Use the preview action on a video card to watch it. Use the download action to save a Wrapper project ZIP that you can keep as a backup or import again later.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I sort my video list?</summary>
					<p>Use the <strong>Sort by</strong> menu to order videos by recently modified, oldest modified, or title. Your selected sort order is remembered on this device.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I copy a video's ID?</summary>
					<p>Yes. Select <strong>Copy</strong> beside the ID on its video card. The ID is copied to your clipboard.</p>
				</details>
			</section>

			<section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-assets">
				<h2 id="faq-assets">Assets and characters</h2>
				<details>
					<summary>Where are my uploaded assets?</summary>
					<p>Open <strong>Settings</strong> and select <strong>Your Library</strong>. You can search, filter by category, preview, and download your uploaded content there.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I upload a character?</summary>
					<p>Select <strong>Upload a Char</strong> in the header and choose a supported character file. To upload audio, images, or other supported assets, use the uploader in Settings.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>What kinds of assets can I import?</summary>
					<p>The editor's file importer accepts common audio files (including MP3, WAV, OGG, WMA, and FLAC), images and SWF files, and MP4 video. After choosing a file, select how to use it when the importer offers categories.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I organize files I uploaded?</summary>
					<p>Open <strong>Settings → Your Library</strong> to search and filter uploaded assets. Select an asset to preview or download it, or use the uploader there to add more files.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I hide themes I don't use?</summary>
					<p>Yes. In <strong>Settings → Video Workspace</strong>, use Theme Visibility to choose which themes appear on the creation page. All themes are enabled by default.</p>
				</details>
			</section>

			<section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-editor">
				<h2 id="faq-editor">Using the video maker</h2>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I choose the video maker's appearance?</summary>
					<p>Yes. In <strong>Settings → Features</strong>, choose <strong>Regular</strong> or <strong>Dark mode</strong> under Video maker interface. This selects which GoAnimate video-maker interface opens.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I change the default theme for a new video?</summary>
					<p>Choose a <strong>Default theme</strong> in Settings. On the creation page, select <strong>Start with your default theme</strong> to open the video maker with that theme.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I change the video's aspect ratio?</summary>
					<p>Yes. Change <strong>Video aspect ratio</strong> in Settings to use 14:9 or 16:9 as the default for the video maker and player.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>What does Show audio waveforms do?</summary>
					<p>This setting controls whether detailed audio waveforms are generated in the editor. Turning them off can improve responsiveness on slower computers.</p>
				</details>
			</section>

			<section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-settings">
				<h2 id="faq-settings">Settings and exporting</h2>
				<details>
					<summary>What does Video Layout change?</summary>
					<p>Video Layout changes how projects are arranged in My Videos. Choose vertical cards or horizontal rows in Settings.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I export a video with GoExport?</summary>
					<p>Install and configure GoExport, then set its executable or <code>main.py</code> path under <strong>Settings → Export</strong>. Select the GoExport action on a video to start an export. GoExport and its required runtime components must be installed separately.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Where are my projects and exports stored?</summary>
					<p>Wrapper stores project data in its configured local save folder. GoExported MP4 files are placed in the <code>Exports</code> subfolder there.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>How do I turn on dark mode?</summary>
					<p>Open <strong>Settings → Appearance</strong> and enable <strong>Dark mode</strong>. Wrapper remembers this choice on this device and applies it to supported pages.</p>
				</details>
				<details>
					<summary>Can I change which browser opens web links?</summary>
					<p>In <strong>Settings → Features</strong>, choose your system default browser or Wrapper's built-in browser for the Google Search, Discord, and Bug Report footer links. The built-in browser also lets you set a profile name to keep its browsing data separate.</p>
				</details>
			</section>
		</main>

		<%~ includeFile("./includes/footer", { env: it.env }) %>
	</body>
</html>
